From: Ziyang Huang <hzyitc@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Sep 2024 16:40:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: split WCSS UserPD contexts with correct
 ownership

Split root and user protection-domain state while validating ASID slots
and unwinding child resources before releasing their remoteproc
contexts. Retain the base driver, clock enablement, IPQ5018 support,
boot arguments and MSA policy as independent patches.

Source-patch: 0806-rproc-qcom_q6v5_mpd-split-q6_wcss-to-rootpd-and-user.patch (6c66dff196cbba8515380110dd3599cde31dd896)
Source-patch: 0807-remoteproc-qcom_q6v5_mpd-fix-UserPD-ownership-and-teardown.patch (0fa7bdb855247b738d1d227d6f4b3417ebdf21a8)

[viking.yfy@qq.com: fold only the direct correction into its feature]
Signed-off-by: Ziyang Huang <hzyitc@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: George Moussalem <george.moussalem@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
